WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.669
MAN: It's impossible
to understand

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:04.571
Bin Laden without reference
to his religious beliefs.

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.373
This was a guy who,
when he was a teenager,

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:09.776
was praying seven times a
day, fasting twice a week.

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:13.146
On the other hand, he
was also a mass murderer.

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:14.748
What was his
relationship to religion?

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:17.384
[music playing]

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.686
Given how religious
Bin Laden saw himself,

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:22.021
it's not a surprise there's
a lot of religious material

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:23.390
on these drives.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:25.759
How great is our last
panel, [inaudible]..

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:27.727
[non-english singing]

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:32.031
MAN: He would
often recite verses

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:35.301
from the Quran in his letters.

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:37.537
He would refer to sayings
of the prophet Muhammad

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:38.338
in his speeches.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:45.578
He thinks he's religious.

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:47.614
He thinks he was
doing the right thing.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:52.318
But he was not a
religious authority.

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:54.788
He was not a graduate
of a seminary

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:58.858
or any kind of traditional
religious training.

00:00:58.925 --> 00:01:03.029
And so we have someone who's
a non-specialist making

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:07.333
unorthodox interpretations
of the faith,

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:11.404
because he actually starts
by acknowledging that Islam

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:19.612
prohibits the killing of
noncombatants in warfare,

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:22.715
but then goes on to
explain, in his mind,

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:27.120
why the political situation
that we are living in

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:30.757
allows him to violate that rule.

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:42.001
What he did was to use
political justifications

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:44.838
to violate a religious edict.

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:47.240
[non-english singing]

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:49.809
MAN: This homemade video
found on the hard drives

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:52.345
begins, as many of these
al-Qaeda videos do,

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:56.249
by quoting a religious verse
with chanting in tandem,

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:57.917
and then the message
becomes clearer.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.329
We hit the United States,
and we scared them.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:16.769
Then inevitably, Bin
Laden himself speaks,

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.304
preaching to his followers.

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:31.251
And I think it's a really
telling piece of propaganda,

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:35.522
how it weaves together
religious imagery

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:39.225
to superimpose
them on the tactics

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:42.161
and actions of al-Qaeda.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:44.297
This homemade
propaganda was crude.

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:46.633
But tragically, it
was also effective.

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:49.869
He was using
religion as a tool.

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:52.772
[non-english singing]

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:03.383
It's a means to control
people, to make people do

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:06.419
whatever you want them to do.

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:10.156
And the ends justify the
means, like any psychopath

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:12.191
can justify anything.

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:15.161
I mean, at one point, he
actually told his commanders,

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:18.631
don't shy away from
shedding blood.

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:20.533
You know, if you
look at the crusade,

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.902
do you think Christianity
is a crusade?

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:24.237
No.

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:26.372
The same thing-- it's
people using religion

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:28.341
to obtain political goals.

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:39.953
I think it's
tragic that we let

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:47.393
a criminal define the religion
of 1.8 billion people.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:52.865
We would never take the word of
the KKK to define Christianity.

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:54.100
It would be ludicrous.

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:57.203
It would be offensive.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:59.806
If the Quran is a
recipe book and it

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:04.844
called for a tablespoon
of sugar in the recipe,

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:08.648
and extremists would read
that and put a cup of sugar

00:04:08.715 --> 00:04:10.049
instead--

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:13.886
so taking what the Quran says
and taking it to its extreme.

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:15.655
Bin Laden didn't do that.

00:04:15.722 --> 00:04:19.192
He read in the Quran, you
need a tablespoon of sugar.

00:04:19.258 --> 00:04:22.895
And instead, he put
a cup of cyanide.

00:04:22.962 --> 00:04:24.430
That's not an extremist.

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:27.200
That's a deviant revisionist.

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:33.473
Bin Laden's view of
his religion and violence

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:35.108
extended to his own family.

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:36.909
Terrorism was the
family calling,

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:40.113
and he was willing to sacrifice
even those closest to him

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:41.714
for his self-styled holy war.

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:44.484
[non-english speech]

